.TH MAT 1 "2026" "mat 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mat \- concatenate files with syntax highlighting and decorations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mat
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.RI [ FILE ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mat
concatenates each
.I FILE
to standard output. With no
.IR FILE ,
or when
.I FILE
is \fB\-\fR, it reads standard input.
.PP
By default mat behaves exactly like
.BR cat (1):
piped and redirected output is plain and byte\-identical to cat. The
.BR bat (1)\-style
frame (line\-number gutter, grid, header, syntax highlighting) is opt\-in via
.B \-\-style
or
.BR \-\-pretty .
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "cat compatibility"
.TP
.B \-n
Number all output lines.
.TP
.B \-b
Number nonempty output lines (overrides \fB\-n\fR).
.TP
.B \-s
Squeeze repeated empty lines.
.TP
.B \-v
Show nonprinting characters using \fB^\fR and \fBM\-\fR notation.
.TP
.B \-e
Equivalent to \fB\-vE\fR (also display \fB$\fR at end of line).
.TP
.B \-t
Equivalent to \fB\-vT\fR (also display TAB as \fB^I\fR).
.TP
.B \-A
Equivalent to \fB\-vET\fR.
.TP
.B \-E
Display \fB$\fR at end of each line.
.TP
.B \-T
Display TAB as \fB^I\fR.
.TP
.B \-u
Ignored (output is always unbuffered). Accepted for POSIX compatibility.
.SS "Decorations (opt-in)"
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pretty
Show the full frame: header, grid, line numbers, and syntax highlighting.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-chop\-long\-lines
Do not wrap long lines (same as \fB\-\-wrap=never\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-style= LIST
Comma\-separated components: \fInumbers\fR, \fIgrid\fR, \fIheader\fR,
\fIheader\-filesize\fR, \fIrule\fR, \fIsnip\fR; or presets \fIplain\fR,
\fIdefault\fR, \fIfull\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-decorations= WHEN
\fIauto\fR, \fInever\fR, or \fIalways\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-color= WHEN
\fIauto\fR, \fInever\fR, or \fIalways\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-wrap= MODE
\fIauto\fR, \fInever\fR, \fIcharacter\fR, or \fIword\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-tabs= N
Expand tabs to \fIN\fR columns in the frame (0 disables).
.TP
.BI \-\-terminal\-width= N
Columns to assume for the frame.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-no\-paging
Disable the built\-in pager.
.TP
.BI \-\-paging= WHEN
\fIauto\fR, \fInever\fR, or \fIalways\fR.
.SS "Line selection"
.TP
.BI \-r " RANGE" "\fR, \fP" \-\-line\-range= RANGE
Print only lines in \fIRANGE\fR. Repeat to accumulate. Forms:
\fIN:M\fR, \fI:M\fR, \fIN:\fR, \fI\-N:\fR (last N), \fIN:+M\fR, \fIN::C\fR (context).
.TP
.BI \-H " RANGE" "\fR, \fP" \-\-highlight\-line= RANGE
Emphasize lines in \fIRANGE\fR in decorated output.
.TP
.BI \-\-squeeze\-limit= N
Maximum consecutive blank lines kept under \fB\-s\fR (default 1).
.SS "Encoding"
.TP
.BI \-\-binary= WHEN
\fIno\-printing\fR (default, skip with notice) or \fIas\-text\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-strip\-ansi= WHEN
\fIauto\fR (strip under highlighting), \fInever\fR, or \fIalways\fR.
.SS "Highlighting"
.TP
.BI \-\-theme= NAME
Color theme. See \fB\-\-list\-themes\fR for available names.
Set a default in the config file.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-themes
Print available theme names.
.TP
.BI \-l " NAME" "\fR, \fP" \-\-language= NAME
Force the syntax to \fINAME\fR.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-list\-languages
Print supported language names.
.TP
.BI \-m " GLOB:NAME" "\fR, \fP" \-\-map\-syntax= GLOB:NAME
Map a filename glob to a syntax name.
.TP
.BI \-\-ignored\-suffix= .EXT
Strip suffix before extension detection.
.TP
.BI \-\-file\-name= NAME
Set display name and syntax detection for stdin.
.TP
.BI \-\-fallback\-syntax= NAME
Syntax when detection fails (default \fIplain\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-detect\-syntax
Print the detected syntax for each input and exit.
.SS "Git"
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-diff
Show git change markers in the gutter
(\fB+\fR added, \fB~\fR modified, \fB_\fR removed).
.SS "Diagnostics"
.TP
.B \-\-diagnostic
Print build capabilities and exit.
.SS "Config"
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Ignore configuration files.
.TP
.B \-\-config\-file
Print the path of the user config file.
.TP
.B \-\-config\-dir
Print the user config directory.
.TP
.B \-\-generate\-config\-file
Print a commented config template.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MAT_OPTS
Default options applied before the command line (also \fBBAT_OPTS\fR).
.TP
.BR MAT_STYLE ", " MAT_TABS ", " MAT_WRAP
Default style, tab width, and wrap mode (\fBBAT_STYLE\fR/\fBBAT_TABS\fR fall back).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, disables color unless forced.
.TP
.B MAT_NO_CONFIG
If set, configuration files are not read.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mat/config
System\-wide configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/mat/config
User configuration (one option per line; \fB#\fR begins a comment).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 on success, 1 if any file could not be read.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cat (1),
.BR bat (1)
